<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sir John asked for a same-day visit. Yesterday morning he woke with chills, aching limbs and a headache, and by the evening he had a fever of 38.8 °C at home and a dry cough. Influenza is going around the dockyard where he has spent his days inspecting the ships. He has no chest pain, breathlessness at rest, confusion or vomiting, and he is drinking well. He has taken amlodipine every day for two weeks and his home readings had fallen to the high 130s; he has taken nothing for the fever. He had an influenza vaccine in the autumn. His exercise treadmill test is booked for two weeks from now. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Sudden, yesterday morning, about 30 hours ago</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Whole body; chest and throat</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>About 30 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Fever, chills, dry cough, aching limbs, headache</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>In bed most of yesterday; up and about today with effort</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Fever highest in the evening</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Influenza among dockyard workers; vaccinated in the autumn; on amlodipine for two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Nothing taken yet</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No breathlessness at rest, chest pain, confusion or vomiting</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

