<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Influenza A (J10.1)</content>. Rapid molecular test positive for influenza A. Uncomplicated influenza within 48 hours of onset in a man of 58 with hypertension and obesity; no sign of pneumonia, and oxygen saturation normal, so no chest film now. [S]<list><item>Oseltamivir 75 mg twice daily for five days.</item><item>Acetaminophen for fever and aches; no ibuprofen or naproxen, which raise blood pressure.</item><item>No decongestants containing pseudoephedrine or phenylephrine, which raise blood pressure.</item><item>Rest at home, fluids, and away from the dockyard until 24 hours without fever.</item><item>Return the same day for breathlessness, chest pain, confusion, or a fever that returns after improving.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension on amlodipine (I10)</content>. Blood pressure acceptable during a febrile illness; amlodipine does not need to be held. [S]<list><item>Continue amlodipine; keep taking home readings once a day.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Expedition preparation (Z71.84)</content>. An exercise test during or just after influenza could be unsafe and misleading. [S]<list><item>Exercise treadmill test postponed until he has been back to his usual activity for at least two weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025); Clinical Practice Guidelines by the Infectious Diseases Society of America: 2018 Update on Diagnosis, Treatment, Chemoprophylaxis, and Institutional Outbreak Management of Seasonal Influenza (2018)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Four-week review in two weeks, or sooner as above. Next scheduled visit 1845-02-24: four-week review after starting amlodipine: blood pressure, side effects, echocardiogram and urine albumin. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
